  "question": "The constraints $x+2y\\leq10$, $2x+y\\leq10$, $x, y\\geq0$, with $Z=x+y$. At which point is $Z$ maximum and what is its value?",
  "answeroption": "C",
  "explanation": "Intersection:<br />x+2y=10<br />2x+y=10<br />Multiply first by 2: 2x+4y=20<br />Subtract: (2x+4y)-(2x+y)=20-10\\implies3y=10\\implies y=10/3<br />x+2(10/3)=10\\implies x=10-20/3=10/3<br /><br />So, $(10/3,10/3)$<br />$Z=10/3+10/3=20/3\\approx6.67$<br /><br />Check at $(0,0),(0,5),(5,0)$<br />At $(0,5):0+2*5=10,2*0+5=5\\leq10$ ok. $Z=5$<br />At $(5,0):5+2*0=5,2*5+0=10$ ok. $Z=5$<br /><br />Thus, $Z$ is maximum at $(10/3,10/3)$, $Z=20/3$.",
  "explanation_image": [],
  "options": {
    "A": "Maximum at $(0,5)$, $Z=5$",
    "B": "Maximum at $(5,0)$, $Z=5$",
    "C": "Maximum at $\\left(\\frac{10}{3},\\frac{10}{3}\\right)$, $Z=\\frac{20}{3}$",
    "D": "Maximum at $(0,0)$, $Z=0$"
